242 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (Iterates over every row of the specified Table and checks the Condition. It returns a new table containing only the rows where the condition is true. It is a fundamental function for row-by-row filtering. Return Value: A table object, typically  used within an aggregator or as a filter  argument. Example: CALCULATE\( [Total Sales],  FILTER\('Sales', 'Sales'[Quantity] > 10\) \) Note: FILTER creates a row context to  evaluate the condition, which can be  performance-intensive on large tables.)
/E (Iterates over every row of the specified Table and checks the Condition. It returns a new table containing only the rows where the condition is true. It is a fundamental function for row-by-row filtering. Return Value: A table object, typically  used within an aggregator or as a filter  argument. Example: CALCULATE\( [Total Sales],  FILTER\('Sales', 'Sales'[Quantity] > 10\) \) Note: FILTER creates a row context to  evaluate the condition, which can be  performance-intensive on large tables.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
