244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (The table equivalent of the CALCULATE function. It evaluates a Table Expression in a context modified by the filter arguments. It does not iterate rows; it changes the filter context. Return Value: A table object, defined by  the original expression evaluated under  the new filter context. Example: COUNTROWS\( CALCULATETABLE\(  'Sales', 'Date'[Year] = 2024 \) \) Use Case: Creating temporary tables based  on modified filter contexts, such as a table  of "High Value Customers" based on a sales  threshold, which can then be counted or  analyzed.)
/E (The table equivalent of the CALCULATE function. It evaluates a Table Expression in a context modified by the filter arguments. It does not iterate rows; it changes the filter context. Return Value: A table object, defined by  the original expression evaluated under  the new filter context. Example: COUNTROWS\( CALCULATETABLE\(  'Sales', 'Date'[Year] = 2024 \) \) Use Case: Creating temporary tables based  on modified filter contexts, such as a table  of "High Value Customers" based on a sales  threshold, which can then be counted or  analyzed.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [17]
>>
